  "term": "obsession",
  "definition": "Historically, obsession referred either to a person’s symptoms being attributed to an evil spirit pressing from outside without inhabiting the body, or to the persistent, irresistible presence of an idea or emotion. In the second sense, it is equivalent to an imperative idea.",
